{"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "find", "ucas": "it(n: u32, a: u32, b: u32) = n % 7 == 0 ? a : b\nfind it 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "find", "points": 1024, "sampled": true, "type": "u32", "model": "gt1030", "peephole": [{"cost": 7, "expr": "3067833783n <= 613566756 ? a : b", "rewrite": "the divisibility test n % 7 == 0 as a multiply and a compare", "holds_where": "n is any u32 (the multiply wraps mod 2^32)", "derivation": "7 is odd, and 7 * 0xb6db6db7 = 1 mod 2^32\nt(n) = n*0xb6db6db7 takes each 32-bit word to a different one (a bijection): a multiply by an odd number does\nthe multiples of 7 are q*7 for q = 0..613566756 (floor((2^32 - 1)/7)); there n * 0xb6db6db7 = q mod 2^32: t takes them onto 0..613566756\na bijection takes every other n outside 0..613566756: t(n) <= 613566756 exactly where n % 7 == 0", "check": "sampled"}], "implementations": []}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "find it: 1024 points (sampled; matches verified on the whole domain), computing in u32, costs from gt1030\n  rewrites the model prices lower (each derived, with what it holds under):\n  cost 7   3067833783n <= 613566756 ? a : b         the divisibility test n % 7 == 0 as a multiply and a compare (derived; checked on a sample)\n      holds where n is any u32 (the multiply wraps mod 2^32)\n      7 is odd, and 7 * 0xb6db6db7 = 1 mod 2^32\n      t(n) = n*0xb6db6db7 takes each 32-bit word to a different one (a bijection): a multiply by an odd number does\n      the multiples of 7 are q*7 for q = 0..613566756 (floor((2^32 - 1)/7)); there n * 0xb6db6db7 = q mod 2^32: t takes them onto 0..613566756\n      a bijection takes every other n outside 0..613566756: t(n) <= 613566756 exactly where n % 7 == 0\n  nothing new up to cost 3 (term bank full)\n  [searched every term up to cost 3: 16384 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}
{"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "find", "ucas": "it(x: u32 in 0..99, y: u32) = x / 10 + y\nfind it 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "find", "points": 1024, "sampled": true, "type": "u32", "model": "gt1030", "peephole": [{"cost": 5, "expr": "(103x >> 10) + y", "rewrite": "the division x/10 as a multiply and a shift in u32", "holds_where": "x in [0, 99] (its range)", "derivation": "M = ceil(2^10/10) = 103, so M*10 = 2^10 + 6\nx*M/2^10 = x/10 + x*6/(10*2^10): the excess is below 1/10 while x*6 < 2^10, and x/10 is at least 1/10 below the next integer, so floor(x*M/2^10) = floor(x/10)\nx <= 99: x*6 <= 594 < 2^10, and x*M <= 10197 < 2^32, so the product does not wrap in u32", "check": "sampled"}, {"cost": 8, "expr": "u32(0.100000001f32(x)) + y", "rewrite": "x/10 on the f32 pipe: the conversion of f32(x) * 0.100000001 (1/10 rounded up to an f32)", "holds_where": "x in [0, 99], inside [0, 2^24), and 99 (0.100000001 - 1/10) + ulp/2 < 1/10: 1.48e-07 + 4.77e-07 < 0.1", "derivation": "x < 2^24 converts to f32 exactly\n0.100000001 = 0x1.99999ap-4 is 1/10 rounded up to an f32, above it by 1.49e-09\nq0 = floor(x/10) is an integer below 2^24, an f32, and f32(x) * 0.100000001 >= x/10 >= q0: the product rounded to nearest is not below q0\nx/10 <= q0 + 9/10, so the exact product is at most q0 + 9/10 + 1.48e-07 (99 times the excess); it is below 16, where rounding adds at most 4.77e-07: it stays below q0 + 1, as 1.48e-07 + 4.77e-07 < 1/10\nthe conversion to u32 truncates toward zero: of a value in [q0, q0 + 1) it is q0 = x / 10", "check": "sampled"}], "implementations": []}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "find it: 1024 points (sampled; matches verified on the whole domain), computing in u32, costs from gt1030\n  rewrites the model prices lower (each derived, with what it holds under):\n  cost 5   (103x >> 10) + y                         the division x/10 as a multiply and a shift in u32 (derived; checked on a sample)\n      holds where x in [0, 99] (its range)\n      M = ceil(2^10/10) = 103, so M*10 = 2^10 + 6\n      x*M/2^10 = x/10 + x*6/(10*2^10): the excess is below 1/10 while x*6 < 2^10, and x/10 is at least 1/10 below the next integer, so floor(x*M/2^10) = floor(x/10)\n      x <= 99: x*6 <= 594 < 2^10, and x*M <= 10197 < 2^32, so the product does not wrap in u32\n  cost 8   u32(0.100000001f32(x)) + y               x/10 on the f32 pipe: the conversion of f32(x) * 0.100000001 (1/10 rounded up to an f32) (derived; checked on a sample)\n      holds where x in [0, 99], inside [0, 2^24), and 99 (0.100000001 - 1/10) + ulp/2 < 1/10: 1.48e-07 + 4.77e-07 < 0.1\n      x < 2^24 converts to f32 exactly\n      0.100000001 = 0x1.99999ap-4 is 1/10 rounded up to an f32, above it by 1.49e-09\n      q0 = floor(x/10) is an integer below 2^24, an f32, and f32(x) * 0.100000001 >= x/10 >= q0: the product rounded to nearest is not below q0\n      x/10 <= q0 + 9/10, so the exact product is at most q0 + 9/10 + 1.48e-07 (99 times the excess); it is below 16, where rounding adds at most 4.77e-07: it stays below q0 + 1, as 1.48e-07 + 4.77e-07 < 1/10\n      the conversion to u32 truncates toward zero: of a value in [q0, q0 + 1) it is q0 = x / 10\n  nothing new up to cost 3 (term bank full)\n  [searched every term up to cost 3: 16384 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}
{"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "find", "ucas": "it(x: u32 in 0..7, y: u32) = (x == 0 ? 3 : x == 1 ? 7 : x == 2 ? 1 : x == 5 ? 9 : 0) + y\nfind it 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "find", "points": 1024, "sampled": true, "type": "u32", "model": "gt1030", "peephole": [{"cost": 6, "expr": "(0x900173 >> (x << 2) & 15) + y", "rewrite": "the map u32(x == 0 ? 3 : x == 1 ? 7 : x == 2 ? 1 : x == 5 ? 9 : 0) of x as a table in one constant (8 entries of 4 bits)", "holds_where": "x in [0, 7] (its range)", "derivation": "u32(x == 0 ? 3 : x == 1 ? 7 : x == 2 ? 1 : x == 5 ? 9 : 0) at x = 0..7 is [3, 7, 1, 0, 0, 9, 0, 0] (evaluated at each of the 8)\nbits [4*i, 4*i + 4) of 0x900173 hold the value at x = i: shifting right by that many bits times x and masking reads it", "check": "sat"}], "implementations": []}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "find it: 1024 points (sampled; matches verified on the whole domain), computing in u32, costs from gt1030\n  rewrites the model prices lower (each derived, with what it holds under):\n  cost 6   (0x900173 >> (x << 2) & 15) + y          the map u32(x == 0 ? 3 : x == 1 ? 7 : x == 2 ? 1 : x == 5 ? 9 : 0) of x as a table in one constant (8 entries of 4 bits) (derived; checked by SAT)\n      holds where x in [0, 7] (its range)\n      u32(x == 0 ? 3 : x == 1 ? 7 : x == 2 ? 1 : x == 5 ? 9 : 0) at x = 0..7 is [3, 7, 1, 0, 0, 9, 0, 0] (evaluated at each of the 8)\n      bits [4*i, 4*i + 4) of 0x900173 hold the value at x = i: shifting right by that many bits times x and masking reads it\n  nothing new up to cost 3 (term bank full)\n  [searched every term up to cost 3: 16384 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}
{"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "find", "ucas": "it(x: u32 in 0..10000000) = x / 7\nfind it 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "find", "points": 1024, "sampled": true, "type": "u32", "model": "gt1030", "peephole": [{"cost": 5, "rewrite": "the division x/7 as a multiply and a shift in u32", "not_proved": "M = ceil(2^19/7) = 74899, so M*7 = 2^19 + 5\nx*M/2^19 = x/7 + x*5/(7*2^19): the excess is below 1/7 while x*5 < 2^19, and x/7 is at least 1/7 below the next integer, so floor(x*M/2^19) = floor(x/7)\nthat and a product below 2^32 need x <= 57343 (the most any shift allows, with 2^19); here x reaches 10000000"}, {"cost": 7, "expr": "u32(0.142857149f32(x))", "rewrite": "x/7 on the f32 pipe: the conversion of f32(x) * 0.142857149 (1/7 rounded up to an f32)", "holds_where": "x in [0, 10000000], inside [0, 2^24), and 10000000 (0.142857149 - 1/7) + ulp/2 < 1/7: 0.0639 + 0.0625 < 0.143", "derivation": "x < 2^24 converts to f32 exactly\n0.142857149 = 0x1.24924ap-3 is 1/7 rounded up to an f32, above it by 6.39e-09\nq0 = floor(x/7) is an integer below 2^24, an f32, and f32(x) * 0.142857149 >= x/7 >= q0: the product rounded to nearest is not below q0\nx/7 <= q0 + 6/7, so the exact product is at most q0 + 6/7 + 0.0639 (10000000 times the excess); it is below 2097152, where rounding adds at most 0.0625: it stays below q0 + 1, as 0.0639 + 0.0625 < 1/7\nthe conversion to u32 truncates toward zero: of a value in [q0, q0 + 1) it is q0 = x / 7", "check": "sampled"}], "implementations": []}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "find it: 1024 points (sampled; matches verified on the whole domain), computing in u32, costs from gt1030\n  not applied (it would cost 5): the division x/7 as a multiply and a shift in u32\n      needs x <= 57343 (it is in [0, 10000000]: its range)\n      M = ceil(2^19/7) = 74899, so M*7 = 2^19 + 5\n      x*M/2^19 = x/7 + x*5/(7*2^19): the excess is below 1/7 while x*5 < 2^19, and x/7 is at least 1/7 below the next integer, so floor(x*M/2^19) = floor(x/7)\n      that and a product below 2^32 need x <= 57343 (the most any shift allows, with 2^19); here x reaches 10000000\n  rewrites the model prices lower (each derived, with what it holds under):\n  cost 7   u32(0.142857149f32(x))                   x/7 on the f32 pipe: the conversion of f32(x) * 0.142857149 (1/7 rounded up to an f32) (derived; checked on a sample)\n      holds where x in [0, 10000000], inside [0, 2^24), and 10000000 (0.142857149 - 1/7) + ulp/2 < 1/7: 0.0639 + 0.0625 < 0.143\n      x < 2^24 converts to f32 exactly\n      0.142857149 = 0x1.24924ap-3 is 1/7 rounded up to an f32, above it by 6.39e-09\n      q0 = floor(x/7) is an integer below 2^24, an f32, and f32(x) * 0.142857149 >= x/7 >= q0: the product rounded to nearest is not below q0\n      x/7 <= q0 + 6/7, so the exact product is at most q0 + 6/7 + 0.0639 (10000000 times the excess); it is below 2097152, where rounding adds at most 0.0625: it stays below q0 + 1, as 0.0639 + 0.0625 < 1/7\n      the conversion to u32 truncates toward zero: of a value in [q0, q0 + 1) it is q0 = x / 7\n  nothing new up to cost 3 (term bank full)\n  [searched every term up to cost 3: 16384 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}
